concept symbols {
  name     = "Symbols"
  summary  = "Identifier-like :name values for tags and enum-like choices, plus symbol_set vocabularies."
  related  = [unions, identifiers]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p <<PROSE
A **symbol** is an identifier-like value written `:name` — no space between the
colon and the name. Symbols are used for tags, enum-like choices, and any time you
want a typed name rather than a string.
PROSE
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
shade  = :amber
accent = :cyan
edge   = :uses
SRC
    }
    h2 "The symbol type"
    p "A free-form field accepting any symbol has type `symbol`. There is no validation on which symbols may appear — anything that lexes as `:name` is valid."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
type Tag {
  name: utf8
  kind: symbol
}

t = Tag { name: "release", kind: :stable }
SRC
    }
    h2 "Symbol sets"
    p "A `symbol_set` names a **closed vocabulary** of symbols. A field typed by the symbol set is restricted to exactly those members, giving an enum-like type without the weight of a union."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
symbol_set Color {
  red
  green
  blue
}

type Paint {
  shade: Color     // only :red, :green, or :blue
}

cream = Paint { shade: :red }
SRC
    }
    p "Use a symbol set wherever you would reach for an enum in another language: severity levels, edge kinds, named layout modes, palette hues."
    h2 "When to use which"
    p "WCL has three closely-related tools for a value that is one of a set of names. The right pick depends on whether the vocabulary is open and whether each variant carries data."
    table {
      header = ["Need", "Use"]
      rows = [
        ["Closed vocabulary, no payload", "`symbol_set`"],
        ["Closed vocabulary with data per variant", "[union](concept_unions)"],
        ["Open string-typed tag", "plain `utf8`"],
        ["Free-form symbol (any `:name`)", "`symbol`"],
      ]
    }
  }
}
